      "headline": "Chief Innovation and Technology Officer, RapidAI",
      "about": "In his role as the Chief Innovation and Technology Officer at RapidAI, Amit leads the R&D, AI development, Product Management, Services and innovation functions at Rapid AI. RapidAI is the global leader in using AI to combat life-threatening vascular and neuro-vascular conditions. Leading the next evolution of clinical decision-making and patient workflow, RapidAI is empowering physicians to make faster decisions for better patient outcomes. Based on intelligence gained from over 7 million scans in more than 2,000 hospitals in over 60 countries, the Rapid® platform transforms care coordination, offering care teams a level of patient visibility never before possible. RapidAI — where AI meets patient care.\n\nPrior to joining RapidAI, Amit held senior executive leadership roles at GE Healthcare, Cisco Systems including technology leadership roles in Networking and Tele-communications as well as embedded systems companies for over 30 years. Amit holds more than 25 U.S. patents in the Networking and Communications space. \n\nBefore joining RapidAI, Amit was a GE Officer,  leading the ~$1.2b digital business for GE Healthcare. As the CDO, Amit was responsible for leading the company’s Digital business, Edison Platform and AI strategy. Amit oversaw GE Healthcare’s complete Digital portfolio, including Enterprise Imaging solutions, Clinical Command Centers and consulting solutions. He was responsible for world wide sales, service, support, product management and engineering. With his 2500+ people global digital team, he also worked to enable the company’s vision for precision health by creating the industry-leading Edison platform, as well as its cloud, edge, device software infrastructure, data strategy, SaaS enablement, artificial intelligence and analytics capabilities. \n\nPrior to his role as the Chief Digital Officer, Amit was the GE Officer and Chief Technology Officer for GE Healthcare Imaging, where he drove digitization, software, digital and cross-modality initiatives across the Imaging business. Amit joined GE Healthcare from Cisco Systems, where he was the India Site Leader and Senior Vice President of Engineering for the Core Software Group, leading product development activities across routing, switching and wireless areas. \n\nAmit has a Master’s degree in electronics and Communication from the Indian Institute of Science.",
